  "notes": "やっぱり confirms expectations or expresses \"after all\".\n\nVARIATIONS:\n- やっぱり: common spoken form\n- やはり: formal/written form\n- やっぱ: casual abbreviation\n\nMEANINGS:\n1. As expected: やっぱりそうだった (it was as I thought)\n2. After all (reversal): やっぱり{行|い}かない (not going after all)\n3. Still/anyway: やっぱり{日本|にほん}がいい (Japan is still best)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- やっぱり{思|おも}った{通|とお}り (just as I thought)\n- やっぱり{無理|むり}だ (it's impossible after all)",
